WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.621 --> 00:00:03.454
- Luck is a process where you move

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:07.160
to luck and you take luck, and you say,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.460
"Come on, luck, I keep you now."

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.101
So when you are free
man, when you have love,

00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:17.101
when you have health, you
are again in paradise.

00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:21.283
- He's the CEO of a
Swiss luxury watchmaker.

00:00:21.283 --> 00:00:23.400
He was previously
successful in rejuvenating

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.021
the Blancpain and Omega brands,

00:00:25.021 --> 00:00:27.143
which are currently owned by Swatch.

00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:29.043
His leadership in the Swiss watch industry

00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:30.938
has single handedly been credited

00:00:30.938 --> 00:00:33.864
as saving the industry
from the quartz movement.

00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:36.003
He's Jean-Claude Biver and here's my take

00:00:36.003 --> 00:00:38.060
on his top 10 rules of success.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.923
Rule number eight is my personal favorite,

00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:42.359
and I'd like to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:44.264
And as always, guys, as
you're watching the videos,

00:00:44.264 --> 00:00:46.344
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:46.344 --> 00:00:48.323
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:48.323 --> 00:00:50.003
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:50.003 --> 00:00:51.160
can be inspired as well.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.158
Also, as you are writing something down,

00:00:53.158 --> 00:00:56.719
it's much more likely to
stick in your head too.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:57.552
Enjoy.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.937
(epic music)

00:01:10.557 --> 00:01:12.058
- Love gives an energy.

00:01:12.058 --> 00:01:14.808
With love, you go to the Everest.

00:01:15.837 --> 00:01:20.253
If you don't have love, which
means passion for the business

00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:24.271
passion is love, if
you don't have passion,

00:01:24.271 --> 00:01:28.438
things are difficult to
achieve in life except normal.

00:01:29.793 --> 00:01:33.070
Without passion, you are in the normality,

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.416
you are like everybody,
you are like a dead fish

00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:39.583
in the road, that fish in the
road swims with the current.

00:01:42.645 --> 00:01:45.410
And in the direction of the
current and in the speed

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.672
of the current, a fish that
is alive goes left, right,

00:01:49.672 --> 00:01:52.243
against the current or with the current,

00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:55.410
so without passion, you are dead fish.

00:01:56.429 --> 00:02:00.046
If I tell you that we have 75 screws

00:02:00.046 --> 00:02:04.210
and that each time the watchmaker
is finished going screw

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.952
and screw, then he should,
during 1/10th of a second,

00:02:08.952 --> 00:02:13.208
when he's finished, I love my
job, then he goes next screw.

00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:17.375
I love this job, the next
one, I love the customer

00:02:19.385 --> 00:02:23.410
who's going to wear it, I love perfection,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.869
if 75 times he's going
to say I love my job,

00:02:27.869 --> 00:02:31.528
I love my customer, I love
my boss, I love my kids,

00:02:31.528 --> 00:02:35.432
I love my wife, he will
leave 75 traces of love

00:02:35.432 --> 00:02:38.829
in the watch and when
he shuts down the case,

00:02:38.829 --> 00:02:42.996
the movement is inside, the
75 traces of love are there.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.088
The universe of passion
is open to everybody,

00:02:48.088 --> 00:02:52.088
but many people don't
know, they believe passion

00:02:53.577 --> 00:02:57.660
should come down from the
sky, no, you go to find

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:03.316
your passion, passion
will not come to you.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:06.483
Is like luck, luck cannot come to you,

00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:11.135
you can buy as many lotto
things, you can make bets

00:03:11.135 --> 00:03:15.302
on Barcelona and Madrid,
luck will never come to you

00:03:16.373 --> 00:03:20.040
but you go to luck,
that's much more secure,

00:03:22.561 --> 00:03:26.173
you go and go to take
luck, if you are in a state

00:03:26.173 --> 00:03:29.293
luck comes down to you,
forget, you will die

00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:33.789
and no luck will have ever
come, luck is a process

00:03:33.789 --> 00:03:36.871
where you move to luck and you take luck

00:03:36.871 --> 00:03:40.151
and you say, come on, luck, I keep you now

00:03:40.151 --> 00:03:43.250
and you take another
one tomorrow and so on.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:46.667
Today, especially in today's environment,

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:51.781
where we have so much competition,

00:03:51.781 --> 00:03:54.864
where speed is so important, we need,

00:03:57.601 --> 00:04:01.351
we definitely need to
always think different,

00:04:03.036 --> 00:04:06.369
in my company, we have a very easy rule,

00:04:09.361 --> 00:04:12.611
whatever we do, whatever, in any field,

00:04:15.638 --> 00:04:19.805
we always try to be the
first and/or to be unique

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:27.263
and/or to be different, and
whatever the project is,

00:04:29.277 --> 00:04:33.444
we have to put the three
conditions and project leader

00:04:35.156 --> 00:04:38.081
or the guy who brings
the idea has to answer

00:04:38.081 --> 00:04:42.248
those three questions, if he
says yes, we will be the first,

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.580
yes, we'll be unique,
yes, we'll be different,

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.740
it's finished, there is no budget anymore,

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:53.823
unlimited budget, no
restriction, he can go ahead

00:04:56.407 --> 00:04:59.100
because whenever you are
the first and different

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:02.933
and unique, you cannot
be wrong, you will win.

00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:07.100
- When you have downtime,
like if something didn't work

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.900
the way you want, what
do you do to get back

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.113
on that positiveness?

00:05:12.113 --> 00:05:13.277
- I talk to the mountain,
I have a mountain

00:05:13.277 --> 00:05:16.321
next to my home that is
called Rocher de Naye,

00:05:16.321 --> 00:05:19.959
it goes up to two, it's very
low, it goes up to 2004,

00:05:19.959 --> 00:05:24.126
2500 meters, or I talk to
the Dovey de Vie mountain,

00:05:25.121 --> 00:05:27.660
which is 4000 mountains,
which is a little further away

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.679
from my home, which I see every morning,

00:05:30.679 --> 00:05:34.657
I see those two mountains and
I say to these two mountains,

00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:38.439
mountains, I have a problem,
but when I look at you

00:05:38.439 --> 00:05:40.860
you are 37 million old.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.417
(men laugh)

00:05:42.417 --> 00:05:44.263
- And I am a little guy.
- You seem to be gay ...

00:05:44.263 --> 00:05:46.839
- I am a little guy here
with a little problem,

00:05:46.839 --> 00:05:51.006
can you help me, and they
will say, come on, look,

00:05:52.175 --> 00:05:55.758
what we have already
seen in so many years,

00:05:56.834 --> 00:06:00.834
your problem is a
nano-problem, come on, get up.

00:06:01.855 --> 00:06:03.377
- Just get up, do it.

00:06:03.377 --> 00:06:04.620
- And whatever, that's it.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:09.201
Many people are what we
call managers, overseers,

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:13.777
and today they can spend seven
years in the watch business

00:06:13.777 --> 00:06:17.516
and eventually then they
might move and be a CEO

00:06:17.516 --> 00:06:20.849
in a car business or in a crystal brand,

00:06:22.839 --> 00:06:27.006
you know, these people are
clever and great entrepreneurs

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:33.646
but they are not necessarily
deeply connected forever

00:06:35.557 --> 00:06:39.474
to one passion, I am
connected just to watches.

00:06:42.876 --> 00:06:46.709
I don't, I would never
like to do another job,

00:06:48.519 --> 00:06:50.493
of course I have other little passions,

00:06:50.493 --> 00:06:54.493
I love wine, I love cheese,
I love classic cars,

00:06:56.343 --> 00:07:00.176
but I would never transform
them in a business

00:07:01.356 --> 00:07:04.533
because my passion is not deep enough,

00:07:04.533 --> 00:07:08.116
while watches is my
life, if I have to die,

00:07:10.994 --> 00:07:13.239
I want people to remember two things,

00:07:13.239 --> 00:07:17.297
I want children and my
wife to remember my love

00:07:17.297 --> 00:07:21.457
and I want people to
remember my contribution

00:07:21.457 --> 00:07:25.036
to the watch business, so
that's really my objective,

00:07:25.036 --> 00:07:28.177
that's why I would never
leave this business,

00:07:28.177 --> 00:07:32.344
and not many, I have been
in the business since '74,

00:07:33.996 --> 00:07:38.163
so it's nearly 40 years, (laughs),

00:07:39.137 --> 00:07:43.134
39 years in the same business,
and I don't know many people

00:07:43.134 --> 00:07:47.092
in this business that
have been 39 years there.

00:07:47.092 --> 00:07:51.259
Some great people came but
they came from a car brand

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.004
or came from Ferrari or
Maserati, and joined the watch

00:07:55.004 --> 00:07:57.447
business and maybe in seven
years they're going to move

00:07:57.447 --> 00:08:00.706
and go to Hermes or
Vuitton, so it's different,

00:08:00.706 --> 00:08:03.373
I am a watch fan, a watch freak.

00:08:05.607 --> 00:08:09.863
It's not enough if you get
help, you must accept help

00:08:09.863 --> 00:08:14.030
and to accept help, you
must be capable of learning.

00:08:16.055 --> 00:08:19.305
And who teach you how to learn, nobody,

00:08:21.415 --> 00:08:25.582
the schools are giving you
every day a spoon of knowledge,

00:08:27.895 --> 00:08:32.013
and you get it in, and
tomorrow another spoon,

00:08:32.013 --> 00:08:35.271
and then you leave university,
but you don't know how

00:08:35.271 --> 00:08:40.068
to learn because you have
been used that they feed you

00:08:40.068 --> 00:08:43.492
with knowledge, but after the university,

00:08:43.492 --> 00:08:46.973
then you have to start to
learn, you have to start

00:08:46.973 --> 00:08:50.890
to learn how to learn
and you have to be humble

00:08:52.243 --> 00:08:55.188
and you must never believe you know it,

00:08:55.188 --> 00:08:59.554
you must have doubts,
the doubt is your friend,

00:08:59.554 --> 00:09:02.971
anybody with little doubts, I'm afraid of

00:09:04.455 --> 00:09:07.590
because these are the dangerous people,

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:11.693
people who drive the car
with no doubts in the fog

00:09:11.693 --> 00:09:16.274
or on the street full
of snow, I am afraid of,

00:09:16.274 --> 00:09:19.441
I want people that have full of doubts

00:09:20.413 --> 00:09:23.671
because the doubt helps you to stay humble

00:09:23.671 --> 00:09:27.511
and helps you every day to ask yourself

00:09:27.511 --> 00:09:31.074
am I on the right track,
what I did yesterday,

00:09:31.074 --> 00:09:35.095
is that right, my vision,
is my vision still okay,

00:09:35.095 --> 00:09:38.830
and if you forget to ask
these questions daily,

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:42.135
one day, pfft, you will
be in the wrong direction.

00:09:42.135 --> 00:09:46.791
So innovation, creativity
at the end of the day

00:09:46.791 --> 00:09:49.458
is more powerful than knowledge.

00:09:51.773 --> 00:09:55.606
Yeah, knowledge is so
easy for anybody to get,

00:09:57.873 --> 00:10:00.311
of course you have to
study, you have to learn,

00:10:00.311 --> 00:10:03.644
but knowledge is there whenever you want

00:10:05.511 --> 00:10:08.008
with the new technology, whatever,

00:10:08.008 --> 00:10:11.853
with all the universities,
knowledge is for everybody

00:10:11.853 --> 00:10:16.020
here, and where is innovation,
where is creativity?

00:10:17.429 --> 00:10:21.179
Innovation and creativity
is above knowledge,

00:10:22.513 --> 00:10:26.633
that is what you put on top of knowledge

00:10:26.633 --> 00:10:28.914
and thank God, innovation and creativity,

00:10:28.914 --> 00:10:33.081
people normally cannot learn,
that gives a huge advantage

00:10:34.578 --> 00:10:37.538
to the ones who are innovative,

00:10:37.538 --> 00:10:39.538
if everybody could learn creativity,

00:10:39.538 --> 00:10:41.394
if everybody could learn innovation,

00:10:41.394 --> 00:10:45.658
we would have to invent
something more or different

00:10:45.658 --> 00:10:48.701
to make the difference between the people

00:10:48.701 --> 00:10:53.021
who have learned something and
the people who are innovative

00:10:53.021 --> 00:10:57.821
so innovation, creativity
is definitely more powerful,

00:10:57.821 --> 00:11:01.079
is much stronger, than knowledge,

00:11:01.079 --> 00:11:05.218
creativity and innovation
is a way of thinking

00:11:05.218 --> 00:11:09.421
and in order to make
people become innovative

00:11:09.421 --> 00:11:12.504
we have created around in our company

00:11:15.131 --> 00:11:18.359
an atmosphere that brings
people to be innovative,

00:11:18.359 --> 00:11:20.797
and the most important atmosphere

00:11:20.797 --> 00:11:24.630
is that you must permit
people to do mistakes.

00:11:27.097 --> 00:11:30.097
If you give bonus for every mistake,

00:11:32.261 --> 00:11:36.161
then people make mistakes,
but they make mistakes

00:11:36.161 --> 00:11:41.101
with a huge pleasure because
they get an additional pay,

00:11:41.101 --> 00:11:43.959
an additional money for every mistake

00:11:43.959 --> 00:11:48.279
and when you ask people
to do a lot of mistakes

00:11:48.279 --> 00:11:52.823
then people become very
active and they trust,

00:11:52.823 --> 00:11:56.099
they start to trust
themselves, the problem is

00:11:56.099 --> 00:11:59.703
in many companies, people
are afraid to be active,

00:11:59.703 --> 00:12:02.359
they are afraid to take
initiatives, they are afraid

00:12:02.359 --> 00:12:06.526
to innovate because
innovation brings uncertainty,

00:12:09.543 --> 00:12:12.962
when you innovate, you
never know, innovation

00:12:12.962 --> 00:12:16.983
is like vision, it's
not reality, the reality

00:12:16.983 --> 00:12:20.141
you have to make it
through later and that,

00:12:20.141 --> 00:12:23.891
to bring people, to take
risks, to be active,

00:12:26.197 --> 00:12:28.583
you can only bring them to that stage

00:12:28.583 --> 00:12:31.916
if you are capable of forgiving mistakes

00:12:33.319 --> 00:12:36.359
and how can you show that
you forgive mistakes,

00:12:36.359 --> 00:12:38.941
you give a little bonus for every mistake

00:12:38.941 --> 00:12:42.242
and I promise you, if you do that,

00:12:42.242 --> 00:12:47.120
little bonus, 100 to 1000
Swiss francs for a mistake,

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.701
if it's a very big mistake, a big bonus,

00:12:50.701 --> 00:12:54.868
if it's a small mistake,
small bonus. (laughs)

00:12:57.498 --> 00:13:00.998
So you see it's also a very innovative way

00:13:03.602 --> 00:13:06.935
of bringing creativity out of everybody.

00:13:09.703 --> 00:13:13.424
Hublot came out with a product in 1980,

00:13:13.424 --> 00:13:16.827
a product that was based on an innovation

00:13:16.827 --> 00:13:20.994
to introduce rubber as a strap,
it seems very common today,

00:13:22.603 --> 00:13:26.436
but rubber in 1980 was
a real courageous move,

00:13:30.224 --> 00:13:34.006
it was even the provocation,
people said hey,

00:13:34.006 --> 00:13:36.006
on a gold watch, rubber?

00:13:36.896 --> 00:13:39.481
Because people didn't know
rubber comes from a tree,

00:13:39.481 --> 00:13:44.107
rubber is natural, rubber
is very comfortable,

00:13:44.107 --> 00:13:47.526
it's very flexible and
rubber is very resistant

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:50.722
and it's waterproof so
finally it's ideal for a watch

00:13:50.722 --> 00:13:55.599
but in those days, people
thought it's a provocation,

00:13:55.599 --> 00:13:59.446
and then Hublot could
not evolve, they stayed

00:13:59.446 --> 00:14:03.279
on a product and I said,
we are not a product,

00:14:06.745 --> 00:14:10.086
we have a message first,
we have a concept,

00:14:10.086 --> 00:14:13.836
and a concept is fusion,
why, because in 1980

00:14:15.526 --> 00:14:18.223
when we put gold together with rubber,

00:14:18.223 --> 00:14:21.104
we created a fusion
because gold and rubber

00:14:21.104 --> 00:14:23.446
never come together, they were together

00:14:23.446 --> 00:14:27.029
only one time in life,
during the Big Bang,

00:14:29.163 --> 00:14:32.827
then everything was in one,
and then rubber went away

00:14:32.827 --> 00:14:35.867
and said, okay, I go now on my tree

00:14:35.867 --> 00:14:38.128
and gold said, okay, I go
and rest in South Africa

00:14:38.128 --> 00:14:40.566
under the earth and
since then they never met

00:14:40.566 --> 00:14:43.733
til people take them and connect them,

00:14:45.344 --> 00:14:49.500
so I said Hublot made a
fusion and fusion must be

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:54.300
our message, must be our
philosophy, must be our religion

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:58.467
and once we have this religion
clear and it is named fusion

00:15:00.753 --> 00:15:03.541
then we can develop further products

00:15:03.541 --> 00:15:06.443
that not necessarily need rubber anymore

00:15:06.443 --> 00:15:10.761
because fusion goes further
away than just rubber,

00:15:10.761 --> 00:15:14.246
it can be carbon, it can
be ceramic, whatever,

00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:18.246
so I was capable to free
Hublot from the product

00:15:21.142 --> 00:15:24.646
and give Hublot a message
and from that message

00:15:24.646 --> 00:15:28.813
new products were born and
that was the most important

00:15:30.406 --> 00:15:33.406
element in the revival of the brand,

00:15:34.848 --> 00:15:38.431
it's to take it away
from a product concept

00:15:40.966 --> 00:15:45.133
and to give it a brand message
and from the brand message

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:51.067
we are then later born
in 2005 new products.

00:15:52.205 --> 00:15:54.203
This guy from that company told me,

00:15:54.203 --> 00:15:57.184
you going to work one year, Mr. Biver,

00:15:57.184 --> 00:16:01.243
and I give you half a
salary, I said, what,

00:16:01.243 --> 00:16:04.326
half a salary, 50%, I said, why,

00:16:06.166 --> 00:16:10.944
I'm going to tell you, because
we not work during one year,

00:16:10.944 --> 00:16:15.024
you will not work, you will
learn, and because you learn,

00:16:15.024 --> 00:16:19.191
somebody must teach you,
and we, my company's going

00:16:20.347 --> 00:16:23.184
to teach you, so you pay me
half of your salary to teach you

00:16:23.184 --> 00:16:27.104
(laughs) These were the good bosses,

00:16:27.104 --> 00:16:29.739
that's the right way to think,
that's what you have to tell

00:16:29.739 --> 00:16:33.302
to the young people, you
come to me, during one year,

00:16:33.302 --> 00:16:35.063
I give you a half salary
because the other half

00:16:35.063 --> 00:16:38.523
you pay me because I teach
you, which is true, by the way,

00:16:38.523 --> 00:16:41.527
that's how it is, but the young people,

00:16:41.527 --> 00:16:44.245
they don't want half salary,
they want full salary,

00:16:44.245 --> 00:16:46.875
okay, then I don't
employ you, stay outside,

00:16:46.875 --> 00:16:49.419
go to another company,
young people must be ready

00:16:49.419 --> 00:16:53.067
to accept half salary,
and they are not ready,

00:16:53.067 --> 00:16:55.264
at least not in the few countries I know,

00:16:55.264 --> 00:16:59.181
so this guy told me, half
salary and no office,

00:17:01.323 --> 00:17:06.144
no secretary, no visit card,
no phone, no traveling,

00:17:06.144 --> 00:17:08.267
no nothing, I said, what will I get,

00:17:08.267 --> 00:17:12.220
you're going to learn, and to
learn you don't need an office

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:14.683
and to learn you don't need a secretary

00:17:14.683 --> 00:17:16.347
and to learn you don't need a phone

00:17:16.347 --> 00:17:18.744
and to learn you don't need a credit card

00:17:18.744 --> 00:17:21.446
and to learn you don't need a name card,

00:17:21.446 --> 00:17:24.696
so I started to learn, and in one year,

00:17:26.203 --> 00:17:29.787
I was there learning, and how do you learn

00:17:29.787 --> 00:17:33.223
when you go in a company,
they put you in an office

00:17:33.223 --> 00:17:37.390
with the director of the
design and then you are there

00:17:39.286 --> 00:17:41.662
and then you sit, and
the guy designs watches,

00:17:41.662 --> 00:17:45.281
and he says, okay, hello, sit there,

00:17:45.281 --> 00:17:48.282
and then you look, and the guy designs

00:17:48.282 --> 00:17:51.323
and after two hours, you
say, what am I doing here,

00:17:51.323 --> 00:17:53.782
I cannot look at this guy
designing all the time,

00:17:53.782 --> 00:17:57.617
so you start to ask questions,
and then the guy said,

00:17:57.617 --> 00:18:02.000
sorry, I have no time, I
must design my watches.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.927
(laughs) Then you tell him,
do you want the coffee,

00:18:03.927 --> 00:18:08.120
and he says, yes, and then
you go and make coffee.

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:13.059
(laughs) You start
becoming very, very humble

00:18:13.059 --> 00:18:16.139
and you don't want to lose too much time

00:18:16.139 --> 00:18:20.523
so you try to take from him,
to take knowledge from him

00:18:20.523 --> 00:18:23.773
and then you tell him, yeah, for lunch,

00:18:26.283 --> 00:18:30.763
can we have lunch together,
they say no, not now,

00:18:30.763 --> 00:18:34.536
I have my wife, yeah, but maybe one day,

00:18:34.536 --> 00:18:37.899
he says, okay, let's
see, and then you have

00:18:37.899 --> 00:18:40.342
one day lunch with him,
and then the guy starts

00:18:40.342 --> 00:18:43.780
to become more open, and one day, you say,

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:47.003
oh, can I invite you
with your wife to my home

00:18:47.003 --> 00:18:50.342
and so I have been one day in the company

00:18:50.342 --> 00:18:54.360
sitting with everybody, with
the director of production,

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.640
with the director of
the after-sales service,

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:00.041
with the director of quality control,

00:19:00.041 --> 00:19:02.080
with the director of the design,

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:05.413
with the director of IT, with everybody,

00:19:07.558 --> 00:19:11.725
with the finance, with
everybody and because of this,

00:19:13.418 --> 00:19:17.501
I learn the basics of the
history of the company,

00:19:19.216 --> 00:19:23.222
but also at the same time,
the history of the watchmaking

00:19:23.222 --> 00:19:27.389
art and after one year, I
knew much, much, much more

00:19:30.822 --> 00:19:33.163
about the history of
making watches, about how

00:19:33.163 --> 00:19:35.739
to make watches, about the
mentality of the watchmakers,

00:19:35.739 --> 00:19:39.403
about the history of the
Swiss watchmaking industry,

00:19:39.403 --> 00:19:43.153
than anybody else because
I had been one year

00:19:45.015 --> 00:19:47.419
just listening to people.

00:19:47.419 --> 00:19:50.567
I had the passion as a
child, which was to play

00:19:50.567 --> 00:19:54.150
with steam machines,
and one day I believed

00:19:55.178 --> 00:19:57.542
that I should take the steam machine

00:19:57.542 --> 00:20:00.918
and I should see how the steam machine

00:20:00.918 --> 00:20:04.168
as an adult can be present, not anymore

00:20:05.139 --> 00:20:08.736
like a steam machine but like a watch

00:20:08.736 --> 00:20:11.558
so I made the transition
from the steam machine

00:20:11.558 --> 00:20:15.725
to the watch, and then the
watch has become my toy

00:20:17.137 --> 00:20:20.720
as an adult, toy of a
child, steam machine,

00:20:21.862 --> 00:20:26.717
toy of the adult, the
watch, and from that day on,

00:20:26.717 --> 00:20:30.884
I entered the watch industry,
and I was free of work,

00:20:32.843 --> 00:20:36.843
I became a free man that
didn't have to work anymore,

00:20:36.843 --> 00:20:40.923
so when you're a free
man, when you have love,

00:20:40.923 --> 00:20:45.090
when you have health, pfft,
you are again in paradise,

00:20:46.055 --> 00:20:50.222
so, I should call myself
paradise man. (laughs)

00:20:55.062 --> 00:20:56.363
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:20:56.363 --> 00:20:59.307
I made this video because
Joe Bordo asked me to,

00:20:59.307 --> 00:21:01.563
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:21:01.563 --> 00:21:03.680
to profile next, leave it
down in the comments below

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.799
and I'll see what I can
do, I'd also love to know

00:21:05.799 --> 00:21:07.659
what did you take from Jean-Claude today

00:21:07.659 --> 00:21:10.101
that had the biggest
impact on you, what message

00:21:10.101 --> 00:21:12.768
hit you the hardest that you're
going to immediately apply

00:21:12.768 --> 00:21:15.200
somehow to your life or
business, leave it down

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.118
in the comments below
and I'm going to join

00:21:17.118 --> 00:21:19.483
in the discussion, I also
want to give a quick shout-out

00:21:19.483 --> 00:21:21.899
to Janina Lee Del Rio,
thank you so much, Janina,

00:21:21.899 --> 00:21:24.619
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:21:24.619 --> 00:21:27.174
I really, really appreciate
all your support,

00:21:27.174 --> 00:21:29.334
so thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:21:29.334 --> 00:21:31.542
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:21:31.542 --> 00:21:35.709
and whatever your one word is,
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:21:42.043 --> 00:21:46.210
- I did a lot in my life, just
because I got a lot of help.

00:21:48.539 --> 00:21:52.706
Help is all you need, and
help, how do you get help?

00:21:56.856 --> 00:22:00.606
The first help is love,
love is all you need.

00:22:03.259 --> 00:22:07.920
It's a song from the Beatles,
all you need is love,

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:11.670
and the day you die,
and you have given love,

00:22:14.237 --> 00:22:19.019
and you have received love,
then that day you can say,

00:22:19.019 --> 00:22:23.579
I was successful, that's
the only measure of success,

00:22:23.579 --> 00:22:27.412
is how much love have I
given to other people,

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:31.237
that's the success and that's life,

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:35.563
we are here for a little
period, and during

00:22:35.563 --> 00:22:38.896
this little period, we have one mission,

00:22:39.862 --> 00:22:42.862
to share, sharing is an act of love,

00:22:46.016 --> 00:22:50.183
try to share, try to think,
a mother shares her body

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:58.603
with all of you, nobody
here in this room is not

00:22:58.603 --> 00:23:02.022
the result of a sharing
process between your mother

00:23:02.022 --> 00:23:06.189
and yourself, if women would
refuse to share their body,

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:11.427
to share their blood,
to share their oxygen,

00:23:13.675 --> 00:23:18.363
nobody would be born
anymore, so we are the result

00:23:18.363 --> 00:23:21.780
of a sharing process, the result of love.

00:23:24.523 --> 00:23:28.690
And that's the rule of life,
and that's all what matters.

